# Copy to .env (git-ignored), fill in, and pass the path: `make run ENV_FILE=.env` or
# `ENV_FILE=.env npm start`. One KEY=value per line, no quotes and no `export` (Docker reads this
# file as it is). Leave all three LLM_* lines empty to run offline on the fixture provider.
# Never commit real values: this example must stay empty.
#
# LLM_NAME      the model name exactly as your endpoint lists it for Apertus v1.5
# LLM_BASE_URL  an OpenAI-compatible base URL, such as https://api.publicai.co/v1, the CSCS
#               inference endpoint, or your own server (http://host.docker.internal:8000/v1
#               reaches a server running on the same machine as `make run`)
# LLM_API_KEY   its key; a server that needs none still needs a non-empty placeholder here
LLM_NAME=
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
# Optional: per-request timeout in milliseconds (default 60000).
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
